# Code owners — SatSandesh
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# docs/CONVENTIONS.md already says "touching a teammate's folder or a
# shared file -- flag it to them first." That was an honour-system rule,
# and in Month 1 it failed silently: a merge removed ~4,100 lines of
# another member's merged, tested code without that member being on the
# review. Nobody did anything malicious -- the rule just had no teeth.
#
# This file gives it teeth. GitHub automatically requests a review from
# the listed owner on any PR touching their paths. Combined with branch
# protection's "Require review from Code Owners" (free on this repo --
# it's public), a PR cannot merge changes to someone's area without
# that person actually seeing it.
#
# HOW TO READ THE OWNERS BELOW
#
# These reflect WHO ACTUALLY AUTHORED WHAT IS IN `main` TODAY -- an
# objective, git-verifiable fact -- NOT a settlement of the open roles
# question (see docs/OWNERSHIP.md § "The unresolved bit"). Once the team
# agrees which role table governs, update this file to match and treat
# THIS file as the enforcement of that decision.
#
# An owner is not a gatekeeper. Anyone may open a PR against any path.
# The owner just has to have seen it before it merges.

